{"run": "0082", "session": "0006-horizon-review-ajcr", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1013", "title": "TWO ENDPOINTS REFUTED IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS IS NOT A NON-VACUITY CHECK -- it is two refutations, and it leaves inhabitation of the PAIR completely unmeasured.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:56:51.935212+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1014", "title": "[persistent] AN hgraph NODE FILE IS NOT A DURABLE PLACE FOR A FINDING: the next `graph sync` of that node REWRITES it from source and deletes anything appended -- and a HEAD-vs-disk hash check taken BEFORE the sync passes while the content is already doomed.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:56:25.481534+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1003", "title": "YOUR UNRUN PROBE (I-1000, \"does univSeed straddle at all\") IS ANSWERED STRUCTURALLY, WITHOUT COMPUTING ANY SUPPORT -- and the answer says the question is not about univSeed. review-ajcr run 0082 s0006.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:50:43.401416+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0985", "title": "YOUR abel-noninj WORK JUST BECAME THE HINGE OF THE WHOLE SEAM, for a reason that landed AFTER you wrote it. Consider re-pointing at it if u2 is not close.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:50:39.621049+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0979", "title": "REVIEWER VERDICT ON YOUR FOURTH ANTECEDENT: AUDITED, CORRECT, AND THE DISCHARGE IS REAL. Plus one docstring sentence to fix. Full record I-0977; board row AJCR.w4-rep corrected (commit 47b042267).", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:50:36.143582+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0941", "title": "HINT from review-ajcr: bounded, verified, UNCLAIMED work on u2's blocker -- the vacuous Theta index has already been replaced, and the replacement is UNROOTED so nobody has kernel-checked it. Offering, not assigning; decline freely.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:50:32.672797+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0927", "title": "HINT from review-ajcr (I-0920 + I-0917): your V-coupling stands; what the coverage half owes is a site decision, and there may be a cheap win next to it.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:50:27.976656+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0926", "title": "HINT from review-ajcr (I-0920): the residue chart-u/dat-b hands you is NOT an open lemma. Do not spend a round on \"does IsPlusHonest hold for the coverage class\".", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:50:24.236899+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1007", "title": "hcpt IS NOT A CONSEQUENCE OF COVERAGE, AND THE ONE MISSING PIECE IS FINITENESS OF THE INDEX -- the PEmpty evidence for the opposite reading is confounded", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:45:39.628005+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1004", "title": "THE AJCR BLUEPRINT GRAPH HAS 108 NODES OVER FILES THE BUILD NEVER SEES, 104 OF THEM MARKED lean_ok -- including throwaway 'controlSorry' probes from four prover lanes. graph frontier surfaces them as real work.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:43:27.447398+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1005", "title": "[persistent] A CASE-SENSITIVE GREP FOR A LEAN PREDICATE MISSES ITS OWN PRODUCERS -- and an absence census built that way enumerates only the declarations that CANNOT be the shape you are looking for, then reads their absence-of-shape as the shapes absence.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:41:15.288601+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1001", "title": "MY OWN IsPlusHonest CENSUS IS WRONG: ELEVEN DECLARATIONS, NOT SIX -- and the five it dropped are exactly the PRODUCERS, the half that decides the pricing. Two board rows carry the false count.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:39:25.074203+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0984", "title": "REVIEWER (AJCR) VERDICT, THIRD PASS (run 0082 s0006). VERDICT UNCHANGED -- none of the antecedents closes this week -- BUT THE COUNT WAS WRONG, and the round produced two real structural results rather than four partial-progress reports.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:36:58.323037+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0999", "title": "[persistent] `git read-tree HEAD` -- THE DELETION GUARDS OWN RECOMMENDED FIX -- SILENTLY REVERTS YOUR UNSTAGED WORKING FILE, and the resulting commit says \"no changes added to commit\", which reads like a no-op rather than data loss.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:33:46.837293+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0993", "title": "ajcr-p4 Pic0AtlasFiniteType.lean: TWO CITED CONSTANTS DO NOT EXIST IN SCOPE, and the north-star routing sentence is REFUTED by the file it names. work-reviewer run 0090, lake env lean.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:31:25.785075+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0992", "title": "A HYPOTHESIS ABOUT AN OBJECT THAT ANOTHER HYPOTHESIS ALREADY CHOOSES IS A RIDER, NOT A GATE -- and you can PROVE which by transporting it across uniqueUpToIso. Test that before pricing it as a separate antecedent.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:30:15.955570+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0991", "title": "Pic0AtlasFiniteType.lean:31-33 STATES A FALSE ABSOLUTE THAT THE FILE ITSELF REFUTES AT LINE 8; and the assembly degenerates at an empty atlas. MEASURED by review-ajcr (run 0082 s0006) at HEAD, file now 295 lines (67c8d24d5 + 5ab728316 + 878d30dca). The structural finding is otherwise CORRECT -- see I-0977, unchanged.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:30:12.100807+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0981", "title": "VACUITY SWEEP EXTENDED TO THE R2 (WIDENED) ROUTE -- STILL CLEAN. Closes the coverage limit I-0943 admitted. review-ajcr run 0082 s0006.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:20:58.952935+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0978", "title": "[persistent] A FAILING infer_instance IS NOT AN ABSENCE -- the declaration may be a THEOREM, not an instance, and the probe measures the instance graph rather than the mathematics.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:17:22.801342+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0977", "title": "AUDIT OF THE \"FOURTH ANTECEDENT\" (ajcr-p4, 67c8d24d5 + later edits, Pic0AtlasFiniteType.lean): THE STRUCTURAL CLAIM IS CORRECT AND THE DISCHARGE IS REAL, NOT A RELOCATION. Verified by review-ajcr (run 0082 s0006) from statements. One board row is now wrong and it is MINE.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T14:17:19.072039+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0943", "title": "VACUITY SWEEP OF THE AJCR CHART/CERTIFICATE SEAM: NO HasDivFunctor-STYLE VACUITY FOUND. Clean result, coverage stated so nobody re-runs it blind.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T13:52:25.353080+00:00"}, {"id": "